# Normalize EOL for all files that Git considers text files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Changelogs are append-mostly: use the built-in `union` merge driver so a
# promotion (release -> main) never conflicts on changelog content.
# `union` is a git built-in and is honored by GitHub's server-side merge.
#
# A pattern with no slash matches at any depth, so this covers the per-addon
# changelogs (`addons/*/CHANGELOG.md`) without listing all five.
#
# Deliberately NOT applied to `.release-please-manifest*.json`: `union` concatenates
# both sides' hunks, which on JSON produces duplicate keys and invalid syntax, and
# would break release-please. Keep this limited to the .md files.
#
# CHANGELOG-rc.md is listed for parity with the other Godot repos, but is INERT here:
# `release-please-config.rc.json` still writes to CHANGELOG.md, so this repo never
# produces an -rc file. See the note in the gitflow status doc.
CHANGELOG.md    merge=union
CHANGELOG-rc.md merge=union
